=== layout: one-panel

# *Selection of Sickle-Cell Alleles*

@body

- Homozygotes for the S allele of the &#61538;-globin gene have sickle-cell anemia.
  - The fitness of SS homozygotes has historically been 0.
- However, in some parts of the world, notably in tropical Africa\:
  - the frequency of the S allele is 0.2 due to moderate selection against homozygotes for A, the wild-type allele_._

=== layout: two-panels

# *Sickle-Cell Anemia*

@left

- AA homozygotes are more susceptible to infection by the parasites that cause malaria than SA heterozygotes.
  - Malaria is widespread in regions of the world where the frequency of the S allele is high.

@right

![Slide image 25](assets/lect15c-natural_selection/image_025.jpg)

=== layout: one-panel

# *Measuring Balancing Selection*

@body

- If the equilibrium frequency of S allele is &#710;p = 0.1, and s = 1.0 because all SS homozygotes die
- We can estimate the intensity of selection against the AA homozygotes due to increased susceptibility to malaria\:
  - &#710;p = t/(s + t)
  - 0.1 = t/(1.0 + t)
    - 0.1(1.0 + t) = 0.1t + 0.1 = t
    - 0.1 = (1.0 &#8211; 0.1)t = 0.9t
  - *t = (0.1)/(0.9) = 0.111*

